# =============================================================================
# experiment/molaro/molaro_T-20_h1.00_8h_a1.34e-2.opts
#
# The committed molaro_T-20_h1.00_2h_a1.34e-2.opts conditions, run four times
# longer and with a log-spaced output cadence. Pair with
# geometry/molaro/molaro_2D_L387um_eps0.35um_axisym_T-20pair_tangent.opts.
#
# WHAT CHANGED AND WHY
# --------------------
# 1. t_final 7.2e3 -> 2.88e4 (2 h -> 8 h). The paired geometry starts from
#    tangent contact with a ZERO neck, so it has to grow through the entire
#    range the pre-necked runs were handed at t = 0 before it reaches anything
#    measurable. The resolution floor for that geometry is r/R = 0.219, a neck
#    WIDTH of 38.1 um -- already past the experiment's 32.81 um starting neck --
#    and a usable fit window needs the neck to roughly double past it.
#
#    8 h is a guess sized off the pre-necked runs, which took 2 h to go
#    33 -> 47.6 um from an ALREADY mature neck; growth from a point contact is
#    fast at first and then slower than that. If the run finishes short of a
#    fittable window, extend rather than reinterpret -- the mesh is only 774k
#    nodes and the whole thing is ~14 core-h, so length is nearly free here.
#
# 2. -t_out_log 60 replaces the default per-step cadence. The deliverable is a
#    slope in log-log, and 8 h at dtmax = 100 s would otherwise trip the
#    1000-snapshot cap into time-uniform output, putting ~90% of the samples in
#    the last decade where the curve is flattest.
#
# Everything else is deliberately IDENTICAL to the 2 h file, so this run and
# the committed pre-necked epsstrict runs differ only in the initial neck:
# same T, same humidity, same alpha_c, same dtmax, same eps in the geometry.
#
# alpha_c = 1.341e-2 from the repo's Arrhenius fit at -20 C, with
#   beta_sub0 = 5.9216e5 s/m, d0_sub0 = 1.0166e-9 m
# (preprocess/comp_eps.py --T0 -20 --alpha 1.341e-2). flag_Tdep is 0, so the
# solver uses these explicitly and rescales beta_sub by rho_vs(T)/rho_ice.
#
# dtmax = 1.0e2 as calibrated for the strict arm (tau_sub = 9.74e1 at
# eps = 3.479e-7, ratio ~1.03). Standing lesson from the cfl1e4 run
# (2026-07-09): the interface-CFL limiter guarantees stability, not rate
# accuracy. Re-run at -dtmax 5e1 before quoting the curve.
#
# WHAT THIS RUN IS FOR
# --------------------
# Not for scoring against the Molaro data -- the pre-necked geometries do that,
# and the answer is in docs/molaro_validation_synthesis.md. This one asks a
# single question: does our model give the SAME growth exponent at 85 um grains
# as at Demmenie's 500 um ones? Kuczynski scaling says m should not depend on
# grain radius. If it does in our model, the two studies cannot be compared and
# that is the more interesting result.
#
# Measure with: python postprocess/neck_width.py <run_dir> --axisym
# Fit with:     python postprocess/fit_neck_growth.py <run_dir>/neck_width.csv --demmenie
# =============================================================================

-t_final 2.88e4                         # 8 h — see note 1 above

-temp -20.0
-humidity 1.00
-grad_temp0 0.0,0.0,0.0

-beta_sub0 5.9216e5                     # K&P beta0 at -20 C, alpha_c = 1.341e-2
-d0_sub0 1.0166e-9                      # physical capillary length at -20 C

-dtmax 1.0e2
-dtCFL 1
-dtCFL_dphimax 0.2

-t_out_log 60                           # log-spaced — see note 2 above
